{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2448","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2448","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2448\",\"parent_revision\":\"a9c0ed0e7a787eec1393fb1e33af925e1a67f4fd132c1c56c5dcd7c0f6c8ed28\",\"root_revision\":\"a9c0ed0e7a787eec1393fb1e33af925e1a67f4fd132c1c56c5dcd7c0f6c8ed28\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Source**: Research entry ./research/coding-agents/pilot-shell.md \u2014 pattern: TDD enforcement hook in /spec implementation phase\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1**: `task_status_hook.py` exists at `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py`\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `ls plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 file exists at path\\nsource: filesystem (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 2**: `start-task/SKILL.md` lines 7-12 register a PostToolUse hook on Write|Edit|Bash\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `grep -n \\\"PostToolUse|matcher\\\" plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 lines 7-12 contain `PostToolUse:`, `- matcher: Write|Edit|Bash`, and the command pointing to `task_status_hook.py`\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md lines 7-11 (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 3**: `task_status_hook.py` does NOT currently contain a `record_tdd_phase(...)` function or any TDD phase logic\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `grep -n \\\"tdd_phase|tdd_violations|record_tdd_phase\\\" task_status_hook.py` \u2014 zero output; function does not exist\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 4**: `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` does NOT reference `tdd_violations[]`\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `grep -n \\\"tdd_violations|tdd_phase\\\" complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 zero output; field not referenced\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 5**: `get_task_context.py` exists as the active-task context reader\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `ls plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/get_task_context.py` \u2014 file exists; marked DEPRECATED in header (use `sam_active_task(action='get')` MCP tool instead)\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/get_task_context.py lines 1-8 (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 6**: `HookProfile` enum exists with MINIMAL/STANDARD/STRICT values in `task_status_hook.py`\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `grep -n \\\"HookProfile|STRICT|STANDARD|MINIMAL\\\" task_status_hook.py` \u2014 class `HookProfile(enum.StrEnum)` with all three values at lines 73-82\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py lines 73-82 (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 7**: pilot-shell.md documents \\\"15 hook registrations across 7 events \u2014 TDD enforcement: RED \u2192 GREEN \u2192 REFACTOR validation\\\"\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `grep -n \\\"15 hook|TDD enforcement\\\" research/coding-agents/pilot-shell.md` \u2014 lines 172-174 contain exact quoted text\\nsource: research/coding-agents/pilot-shell.md lines 172-174 (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 8**: Language manifests declare `test_patterns` (e.g., `[\\\"tests/**/*.py\\\", \\\"test_*.py\\\", \\\"*_test.py\\\"]`)\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: `grep -n \\\"test_patterns\\\" plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml` \u2014 line 8 declares `test_patterns: [\\\"tests/**/*.py\\\", \\\"test_*.py\\\", \\\"*_test.py\\\"]`\\nsource: plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml line 8 (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 9**: Active-task context JSON at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-{session_id}.json` \u2014 format confirmed\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nevidence: task_status_hook.py docstring lines 19-22 describe the context file mechanism; `get_context_file_path()` at line 265-280 builds the path using `_dh_paths.context_dir() / f\\\"active-task-{session_id}.json\\\"`\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py lines 265-280 (verified 2026-05-29)\\n\\n**Claim 10**: INCONCLUSIVE \u2014 Hook access to test exit codes when Bash is invoked via Agent sub-call\\nevidence: PostToolUse hook receives tool output when Bash is called directly; when Bash is invoked via Agent sub-call the sub-agent's Bash output may not be visible to the parent PostToolUse hook. Investigation required.\\nsource: Unable to verify from static analysis alone \u2014 requires runtime observation\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Enforce RED to GREEN to REFACTOR TDD phase via task_status_hook, not as documented norm\\nDate: 2026-05-29\\nGoal: Extend the PostToolUse hook to mechanically enforce the TDD phase sequence (red\u2192green\u2192refactor) and surface violations in the complete-implementation quality gate.\\nConditions:\\n1. task_status_hook.py exists and handles PostToolUse Write|Edit|Bash events | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: `ls` output \u2014 file confirmed at plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py\\n2. Active-task context JSON mechanism exists at ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-{session_id}.json | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: task_status_hook.py lines 265-280\\n3. get_task_context.py exists as the active-task context reader | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: ls confirmed; DEPRECATED header at lines 1-8\\n4. start-task/SKILL.md frontmatter registers the PostToolUse hook (lines 7-12 confirmed) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: grep output \u2014 lines 7-11\\n5. complete-implementation/SKILL.md is the consumer of tdd_violations[] findings | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: file confirmed; tdd_violations[] will be added as new input\\n6. HookProfile enum exists with MINIMAL/STANDARD/STRICT values | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: task_status_hook.py lines 73-82\\n7. Config storage location for strict-mode TDD enforcement flag | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE env var pattern already established at lines 76, 92-107\\n8. Test file detection patterns when no language manifest active | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: python3/language-manifest.yaml line 8 \u2014 test_patterns declared; schema documents patterns for all 5 language types\\n9. Hook access to test exit codes when Bash via Agent sub-call | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Citation: fact-checker INCONCLUSIVE \u2014 not blocking; documented limitation for v1\\n10. Active-task JSON schema fields tdd_phase + tdd_violations[] not yet defined | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: task_status_hook.py lines 295-308 show JSON read/write pattern\\n11. Language manifest test_patterns field | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: language-manifest-schema.md line 109; python3/language-manifest.yaml line 8\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 7 (Config storage): MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE \u2014 established env var pattern exists\\n- Condition 8 (Test file detection): MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE \u2014 language manifests declare test_patterns; fallback derivable\\n- Condition 9 (Agent sub-call exit code): MISSING \u2192 DERIVABLE \u2014 not blocking; v1 limitation acceptable\\n- Condition 10 (active-task JSON schema): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE \u2014 extension pattern confirmed\\n- Condition 11 (language manifest patterns): DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE \u2014 confirmed by source files\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Priority**: P1 (should-have)\\n\\n**Rationale**: TDD enforcement is a process guardrail that improves code quality and makes violations observable. Without it, TDD compliance depends entirely on agent adherence to the `test-failure-mindset` skill. The hook adds mechanical enforcement to an existing documented norm. P1 reflects: high value (audit trail, enforcement, review gate integration), medium urgency (not blocking active work), and no external dependencies.\\n\\n**Effort**: Medium \u2014 hook script extension (~150-200 LOC) + active-task JSON schema change (backward-compatible) + `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` update + config mechanism design. Hook firing infrastructure already in place; new logic is the TDD phase state machine and test file detection.\\n\\n**Blocking items**: None \u2014 `task_status_hook.py` and active-task context JSON mechanism already exist. #2445 may benefit from this hook but can proceed without it.\\n\\n**Target timing**: No hard deadline. Natural fit alongside any implementation task work session where agent TDD compliance visibility is being improved.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: None directly.\\n- Bottleneck: Without this hook, TDD compliance in `implement-feature` depends entirely on the agent following the norm from `test-failure-mindset` skill. Compliance is inconsistent and untracked. `complete-implementation` has no data about TDD violations because nothing records them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Makes TDD enforcement observable \u2014 `tdd_violations[]` in task artifact creates an audit trail.\\n- Enables `complete-implementation` to surface TDD violations as review findings.\\n- Warning mode provides lightweight feedback without blocking; strict mode (exit code 2) provides hard enforcement for teams that require it.\\n- Aligns with pilot-shell.md's hook-based TDD enforcement: \\\"15 hook registrations across 7 events \u2014 TDD enforcement: RED \u2192 GREEN \u2192 REFACTOR validation\\\".\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nOn `Write/Edit` to a test file (matching test patterns): if `phase == \\\"red\\\"`, record the test file path in active-task context.\\n\\nOn `Bash` command matching test runner patterns (`pytest`, `npm test`, `go test`, etc.): parse exit code; if non-zero AND a test file was edited in this phase, transition `phase` to `green` (implementation edits now permitted).\\n\\nOn `Write/Edit` to a non-test source file: if `phase == \\\"red\\\"` (no failing test recorded yet for this task), emit a non-blocking warning via stderr and record the violation in task artifact under `tdd_violations[]`. With the strict config flag active, exit with code 2 to block the edit.\\n\\n`complete-implementation` reads `tdd_violations[]` from the task artifact and surfaces any entries as review findings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nExtend `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` with a `record_tdd_phase(...)` function, OR add a sibling script `tdd_phase_hook.py` if separation is preferred. The active-task JSON schema gains a `tdd_phase` field (one of `red | green | refactor`) and a `tdd_violations[]` array. The hook is registered in `start-task/SKILL.md` frontmatter as an additional `PostToolUse` hook entry.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Either `tdd_phase_hook.py` exists at `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/tdd_phase_hook.py`, OR `task_status_hook.py` contains a function named `record_tdd_phase(...)`.\\n2. Active-task JSON at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-*.json` contains a `tdd_phase` field after the first `Write|Edit` tool call in a task.\\n3. `cat ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-*.json | jq .tdd_violations` returns an array (empty or populated) \u2014 not `null`.\\n4. After a `Write/Edit` to a non-test source file when `tdd_phase == \\\"red\\\"`, `tdd_violations[]` contains at least one entry.\\n5. `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` references `tdd_violations[]` as an input to its review findings step.\\n6. The strict-mode config mechanism is documented: either as env var `DH_TDD_ENFORCE=strict` or a `.dh/config.yaml` key \u2014 one approach is chosen and documented, not left open.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` (existing hook \u2014 confirmed at this path) |\\n| Skill | /dh:start-task (registers the PostToolUse hook \u2014 frontmatter lines 7-12 confirmed) |\\n| Skill | /dh:test-failure-mindset (reasoning aid \u2014 not enforcement; this item adds enforcement) |\\n| Skill | /dh:complete-implementation (consumer of `tdd_violations[]` findings) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/get_task_context.py` (active-task context reader \u2014 schema extension needed here) |\\n| External pattern | pilot-shell.md \u00a7Quality Hooks \u2014 \\\"15 hook registrations across 7 events; TDD enforcement: RED \u2192 GREEN \u2192 REFACTOR validation\\\" |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 `task_status_hook.py` and the active-task context JSON mechanism already exist.\\n- Blocks: #2445 (/dh:fix would benefit from this hook for mechanical RED enforcement at step 2, but #2445 can be built without it).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 hook script extension (or new sibling script) + active-task JSON schema change + `complete-implementation` findings integration + config mechanism design. The hook firing mechanism is already in place; the new logic is the TDD phase state machine and test file detection.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:2347fa7aac8dd86c064552df26f9c825 -->\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/test-failure-mindset/SKILL.md` \u2014 currently a reasoning aid; should reference that the TDD phase hook now records violations automatically, so agents have observable data rather than relying on memory.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` \u2014 hook profile documentation must include the new TDD enforcement flag and how to enable warning vs strict mode.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 reads `tdd_violations[]` from task artifact as a review finding; currently has no reference to this field; must gain a section describing how to surface violations.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/get_task_context.py` \u2014 reads `active-task-*.json`; the schema extension (`tdd_phase`, `tdd_violations[]`) is backward-compatible but consumers reading these fields must handle the case where they are absent (pre-hook sessions).\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_config.py` \u2014 if `.dh/config.yaml` is chosen as the config location for the strict-mode flag, `dh_config.py` must expose a new config key reader (e.g. `tdd.enforce`).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/plugins/python3-development/manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml` \u2014 already declares `test_patterns: [\\\"tests/**/*.py\\\", \\\"test_*.py\\\", \\\"*_test.py\\\"]`; the hook should consume this field to drive test file detection when a manifest is active.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 the primary hook script; either gains a `record_tdd_phase(...)` function or spawns/calls the sibling hook; must accept `tdd_phase` and `tdd_violations` as fields in the active-task context JSON write path.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/tdd_phase_hook.py` (new, if separation chosen) \u2014 owns the TDD phase state machine; writes to active-task context JSON.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` frontmatter (hooks block) \u2014 if sibling hook chosen, a new PostToolUse hook entry must be added; `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` path expansion is already established.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe item's design intent \u2014 extend `task_status_hook.py` to enforce TDD phases via the existing PostToolUse hook mechanism \u2014 is fully aligned with the current implementation architecture.\\n\\n**Supporting evidence**:\\n\\n1. `task_status_hook.py` already uses the established pattern for reading `CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE` from environment and dispatching profile-specific behavior (lines 73-107). The proposed `DH_TDD_ENFORCE` flag or `CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE=strict` extension follows this exact same pattern.\\n\\n2. The active-task context JSON schema at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-{session_id}.json` is already read/written by the hook (lines 265-308). Adding `tdd_phase` and `tdd_violations[]` fields is a backward-compatible schema extension using the same JSON I/O path.\\n\\n3. `start-task/SKILL.md` frontmatter already has a `hooks:` block with `PostToolUse: [matcher: Write|Edit|Bash]`. A second hook entry in the same block is idiomatic.\\n\\n4. `HookProfile.STRICT` already exists and gates `run_strict_pre_completion_checks()` (lines 971-973). Adding TDD phase checks under `STRICT` or a dedicated TDD config flag follows the same pattern.\\n\\n**Divergence notes**: None identified.\\n\\nThe implementation approach described in the item (extension vs sibling script, config flag location) represents design choices within the aligned architecture \u2014 not divergence from design intent. The three open questions in the item are implementation decisions, not architectural misalignments.\\n\\n**Affected systems status**:\\n- `task_status_hook.py`: no TDD logic currently \u2014 clean extension point\\n- `complete-implementation/SKILL.md`: no tdd_violations reference \u2014 clean extension point\\n- `test-failure-mindset/SKILL.md`: reasoning-only guidance, no hook reference \u2014 update needed to reference auto-recording\\n- `implementation-manager/SKILL.md`: documents hook profiles \u2014 will need new TDD section added\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` \u2014 documents `CLAUDE_SKILLS_HOOK_PROFILE` and hook profiles; must document the new `DH_TDD_ENFORCE` env var or `.dh/config.yaml tdd.enforce` key and the new `task-tdd-phase` hook ID if a sibling hook is registered.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 registers the PostToolUse hook in frontmatter; if a sibling `tdd_phase_hook.py` is added, a second `PostToolUse` entry must be added to the frontmatter `hooks:` block.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 must reference `tdd_violations[]` as an input to the quality gate findings step.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface (tdd_violations[] handling)\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated (start-task, implementation-manager, complete-implementation, test-failure-mindset)\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-17T12:43:04.337883Z</sub>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- File `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/tdd_phase_hook.py` exists, or task_status_hook.py contains a function `record_tdd_phase(...)`\\n- Active-task JSON at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-*.json` contains a `tdd_phase` field after one edit\\n- Running `cat ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/active-task-*.json | jq .tdd_violations` returns an array after an implementation-without-test edit\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nstart-task/SKILL.md lines 6\u201312 register a single `PostToolUse` hook firing on Write|Edit|Bash that runs task_status_hook.py. This hook updates task metadata after edits but does NOT enforce the TDD RED\u2192GREEN\u2192REFACTOR sequence: an agent can write implementation code with no preceding failing test, and the hook will accept it. There is a `test-failure-mindset` skill and an `analyze-test-failures` skill that prescribe reasoning, but no executable hook gate that refuses an implementation Edit when no preceding test file edit (with a failing-test run) has been recorded for the same task.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Risk Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nHigh overall. Two critical paths: (1) `task_status_hook.py` is the central hook \u2014 incorrect TDD phase transitions silently corrupt task state for all running tasks; (2) `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` gate change rejects previously-acceptable task completions if `tdd_violations[]` is non-empty. Active-task JSON schema extension is backward-compatible (new keys, no removals) but any consumer that strict-validates the schema must be updated. Dependency order: hook implementation ships first; complete-implementation gate change ships after violations array is reliably populated.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nExtend task_status_hook.py (or add sibling tdd_phase_hook.py) to record per-task phase state in active-task context JSON: `phase: red | green | refactor`. Hook behavior:\\n\\n- On Write/Edit to test file (matching repo test patterns from language manifest): if `phase == \\\"red\\\"`, record test file path.\\n- On Bash command matching `pytest|npm test|go test|...`: parse exit code; if non-zero AND test file was edited in this phase, transition to `phase: green` (allow implementation edits next).\\n- On Write/Edit to non-test source file: if `phase == \\\"red\\\"` (no failing test recorded yet), emit non-blocking warning via stderr and record violation in task artifact (`tdd_violations[]`). With config flag, refuse edit by exit code 2.\\n\\ncomplete-implementation quality gate reads `tdd_violations[]` from task artifact and surfaces them as a review finding.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| System | File/Path | Change Type | Risk |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Task status hook | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/task_status_hook.py` | MODIFY \u2014 extend with TDD phase state machine | High \u2014 primary hook; incorrect state transitions affect all task executions |\\n| TDD phase hook (option) | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/tdd_phase_hook.py` (new) | CREATE (if separation chosen) | Medium \u2014 new hook; requires hooks.json registration |\\n| Active-task context JSON | `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/active_task.json` (runtime) | SCHEMA EXTENSION \u2014 add `tdd_phase`, `tdd_violations[]` | Medium \u2014 existing consumers reading the schema must tolerate new keys |\\n| complete-implementation skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` | MODIFY \u2014 read `tdd_violations[]` before gate | High \u2014 changes completion acceptance criteria for all tasks |\\n| start-task skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` | MODIFY \u2014 hook registration step | Low \u2014 documentation; hook is registered via hooks.json not skill prose |\\n| Python language manifest | `plugins/development-harness/skills/language-manifests/python3/language-manifest.yaml` | REFERENCE (test file patterns) | None \u2014 read-only; patterns used by hook to detect test files |\\n| DH config | `plugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_config.py` | POSSIBLE MODIFY \u2014 new config key | Low \u2014 additive; defaults prevent breakage |\\n| implementation-manager skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/SKILL.md` | MODIFY \u2014 document new TDD behavior | Low \u2014 documentation; no runtime effect |\\n| test-failure-mindset skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/test-failure-mindset/SKILL.md` | MODIFY \u2014 reference auto-recording | Low \u2014 cross-reference documentation |\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b43c54b8b79a83b6125779655f9616843e3dce80783edc7ea7198d74135572b3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTAh6A\"}"}